From 90f07f61880c12ee69700653b4cff8b5d6993881 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:11:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] fix(cli): carry a provider failure's structure into the
 ACP error data

Every failed Cline turn ended session/prompt with JSON-RPC -32603 and data {message}
alone, so a harness that must tell a throttle from an outage from a model that is not
ready could only match text. The AWS exception name, HTTP status, retryability,
retry-after and attempt count were all known where the error was raised and dropped by
the time it was flattened to a string.

describeProviderError (llms) reads them from the error the AI SDK raised: the exception
name from x-amzn-errortype, a JSON __type or an AWS SDK style name; the status from the
APICallError or $metadata; isRetryable from the SDK flag, the status, or the exception
name; retry-after from retry-after-ms or retry-after (seconds or an HTTP date); attempts
from a RetryError; and a network code (ECONNRESET, ETIMEDOUT, Bun's ConnectionClosed).
Nothing is inferred from message text and no status is synthesised.

The model boundary carries the result on the finish event as errorDetails (with a phase:
request or stream). The agent runtime keeps it on the error the run fails with
(ProviderTurnError, ContextWindowOverflowError), so it is attached by identity and never
to an unrelated failure; an error thrown from prepareTurn (the compaction summary call)
carries the details of the finish event it came from, or is described by its own AI SDK
fields, with phase compaction. run-failed and the public error event carry it, and
acpAgent puts it in the JSON-RPC error data next to the unchanged message: errorName,
statusCode, isRetryable, retryAfterS, attempts, code, stopReason, phase, and errorClass
when it is not unknown.

stopReason model_context_window_exceeded (the AI SDK's rawFinishReason) ended the turn as
a clean end_turn, so a full window was invisible over ACP. It now ends the turn as an
error, errorName ModelContextWindowExceeded, and the overflow recovery does not replay it:
its text has already reached the client.

A bun patch for @ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock 5.0.62 keeps the exception type of a ConverseStream
exception frame inside an HTTP 200 as __type on the error part; the provider dropped it.

Two existing gateway assertions gain the errorDetails their 400 errors now carry.
